{"surah": 111, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "تَبَّتْ يَدَآ أَبِى لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ ", "translation": "May the hands of Abū Lahab be ruined, and ruined is he.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَبَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّbَt", "root": "تبب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَدَآ", "translit": "ٓāَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَبِى", "translit": "àِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهَبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَhَl", "root": "لهب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَتَبَّ", "translit": "َّbَtَw", "root": "تبب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "مَآ أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُۥ وَمَا كَسَبَ ", "translation": "His wealth will not avail him or that which he gained.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَغْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْغَaʾ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَالُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُlāَm", "root": "مول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَسَبَ", "translit": "َbَsَk", "root": "كسب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "سَيَصْلَىٰ نَارًا ذَاتَ لَهَبٍ ", "translation": "He will [enter to] burn in a Fire of [blazing] flame", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَيَصْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْṣَyَs", "root": "صلي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَارًا", "translit": "āًrāَn", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَاتَ", "translit": "َtāَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهَبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَhَl", "root": "لهب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَٱمْرَأَتُهُۥ حَمَّالَةَ ٱلْحَطَبِ ", "translation": "And his wife [as well] - the carrier of firewood.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱمْرَأَتُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُtَaʾَrْmٱَw", "root": "مرا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حَمَّالَةَ", "translit": "َẗَlāَّmَḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْحَطَبِ", "translit": "ِbَṭَḥْlٱ", "root": "حطب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فِى جِيدِهَا حَبْلٌ مِّن مَّسَدٍۭ ", "translation": "Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جِيدِهَا", "translit": "āَhِdyِjg", "root": "جيد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَبْلٌ", "translit": "ٌlْbَḥ", "root": "حبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّسَدٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭdَsَّm", "root": "مسد"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "عيسى وكنى أعداءه فقال {تبت يدا أبي لهب} وأما قولك جلست بإزائي فإني سمعت أمير المؤمنين عليا رضي الله عنه يقول إذا أردت أن تنظر إلى رجل من أهل النار فانظر إلى رجل جالس وحوله قوم قيام فقال له هشام عظني فقال سمعت من أمير المؤمنين علي رضي الله عنه يقول إن في جهنم حيات كالقلال وعقارب كالبغال تلدغ كل أمير لا يعدل في رعيته ثم قام وهرب وعن سفيان الثوري رضي الله عنه قال أدخلت على أبي جعفر المنصور بمنى فقال لي ارفع إلينا حاجتك فقلت له اتق الله فقد ملأت الأرض ظلما وجورا قال فطأطأ رأسه ثم رفعه ف", "english": "As for supplicating for him, it is not lawful except to say: \"May God set you aright,\" or \"May God grant you success in good deeds,\" or \"May God prolong your life in His obedience,\" or whatever runs in this course. As for supplicating for his protection, long continuance, and the lavishness of divine favor, along with addressing him as \"My master\" (al-mawlā) and what is in its meaning, that is not permissible. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: {«Whoever supplicates for the continuance of a tyrant has loved that God be disobeyed in His earth»} (1)", "book_title": "The Lawful and Prohibited", "section_title_ar": "Section 391", "section_title_en": "On the Etiquette of Entering Upon Tyrannical Rulers and the Obligation of Forbidding Wrong", "section_index": 391, "anchors": "- Root: ظلم (ẓ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is to place something in other than its proper place; darkness (ẓulmah) as the privation of light.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ẓulm (injustice/tyranny) is the act of transgressing the proper boundary (ḥadd) and placing a thing in other than its due locus; it is a form of spiritual darkness.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): to act unjustly. Metaphorical (majāz): \"A land that has been wronged\" (arḍ maẓlūmah) meaning never dug or cultivated—thus the tyrant leaves the land of justice barren and uncultivated.\n- Root: سكن (s-k-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be still, to rest, to dwell; the opposite of motion and agitation.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Sukūn (silence/rest) can be praiseworthy when it is a cessation from falsehood, or blameworthy when it is an abandonment of an obligatory act of forbidding wrong.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical stillness. Metaphorical: the silence of the tongue from speaking the truth, which is a blameworthy stillness of the heart's faculty of command.\n- Root: أمر (a-m-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To command; a matter, affair, or situation.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-amr bi-al-maʿrūf (commanding the right) is the obligation to enjoin what is recognized as good by the Sacred Law and sound reason.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to issue a command. Metaphorical: the \"command\" (amr) of a thing is its very essence or situation, as in \"the matter of the polity\" (amr al-siyāsah).\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Focused Predication (Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā) — Used to restrict predicates to specific subjects, as in the author's exclusive focus on the conditions and obligations of entering upon rulers.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'The Lawful and Prohibited'", "badge": "Hadith"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 230, 1157], [2, 1157, 4000], [3, 4000, 4939], [4, 4939, 5656], [5, 5656, 6930]], "111:1": [[1, 230, 1157], [2, 1157, 4000], [3, 4000, 4939], [4, 4939, 5656], [5, 5656, 6930]], "2": [[1, 400, 2180], [2, 2180, 3399], [3, 3399, 4015], [4, 4015, 5110], [5, 5110, 6303], [6, 6303, 6910]], "111:2": [[1, 400, 2180], [2, 